.TH "RECORD\-EXPORT\-DATABASE\.PY" "" "March 2026" ""
.SH "NAME"
\fBrecord\-export\-database\.py\fR
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBrecord\-export\-database\.py\fR \fBoutput_file\fR
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBrecord\-export\-database\.py\fR exports the configured RECORD database to the named output file\.
.P
If the configured database type is Gremlin, the command connects to the graph database, retrieves all vertices and edges, converts map keys to strings where needed, and writes the result as formatted JSON\.
.P
If the configured database type is not Gremlin, the command invokes \fBpg_dump\fR to create a PostgreSQL custom\-format backup in the named output file\.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fBoutput_file\fR
path to the file to create
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Returns 0 on success\.
.P
Returns non\-zero if the database export fails, if the database connection cannot be made, or if \fBpg_dump\fR exits with an error\.
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
The command uses the RECORD database configuration provided by the local Python \fBrecord\fR module\.
.SH "RETURN VALUE"
None\.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
Export a Gremlin database or PostgreSQL backup to the named file:
.IP "" 4
.nf
record\-export\-database\.py export\.json
.fi
.IP "" 0
.P
Create a PostgreSQL custom\-format dump:
.IP "" 4
.nf
record\-export\-database\.py backup\.dump
.fi
.IP "" 0
.SH "FILES"
.TP
\fBlib/record\.py\fR
provides database configuration and connection handling
